From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 08:50:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: Unbind vertex buffer slots set with no views.

IASetVertexBuffers with pViews == NULL returned early, so the slots kept
their earlier views. It now clears StartSlot..StartSlot+NumViews and
marks the table dirty: the slots read zeros through the null vertex
buffer, widened by the format, as unbound slots do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/d3d12/d3d12_command_list.cpp | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d12/d3d12_command_list.cpp b/src/d3d12/d3d12_command_list.cpp
index acc5bb7..273eb19 100644
--- a/src/d3d12/d3d12_command_list.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d12/d3d12_command_list.cpp
@@ -1550,11 +1550,9 @@ public:
   void STDMETHODCALLTYPE
   IASetVertexBuffers(UINT StartSlot, UINT Count, const D3D12_VERTEX_BUFFER_VIEW *Views) {
     DXMT_STAT_SCOPE("list.IASetVertexBuffers");
-    if (!Views)
-      return;
-    
+    // MacNeutron: no views unbinds the slots, which then read zeros (measured: D3DMetal ignores such a call).
     for (unsigned Slot = StartSlot; Slot < StartSlot + Count; Slot++) {
-      vertex_buffers_[Slot] = Views[Slot - StartSlot];
+      vertex_buffers_[Slot] = Views ? Views[Slot - StartSlot] : D3D12_VERTEX_BUFFER_VIEW{};
     }
     dirty_state_.set(DirtyState::VertexBuffer);
   };
